-# ClanGrindHeatmap
-ClanGrindHeatmap OSRS plugin+# Clan Grind Heatmap
+
+Clan Grind Heatmap is a RuneLite external plugin that is being prepared to show when your clan is most actively gaining XP. The current implementation establishes the plugin shell, configuration, metadata, and pure-Java heatmap bucketing logic so it is ready for manual RuneLite testing before deeper Wise Old Man/TempleOSRS integration.
+
+## Purpose
+
+The plugin is intended to help clan leaders and members answer questions like:
+
+- Which hours of the day are clan members most active?
+- Are recent XP gains clustered around events, bossing nights, or competitions?
+- What time windows are best for scheduling clan activities?
+
+## Current features
+
+- RuneLite plugin descriptor and `runelite-plugin.properties` metadata for Plugin Hub preparation.
+- Configurable tracking window and active-hour threshold.
+- Optional login chat message confirming the plugin is enabled.
+- Pure Java heatmap model helpers for bucketing XP gain events by UTC hour and converting counts to 0-100 intensity values.
+- JUnit smoke tests for descriptor metadata and heatmap model behavior.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Setting | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Show Login Message | Enabled | Prints a game chat message after login so manual testers can confirm the plugin loaded. |
+| History Days | 7 | Number of days that future activity collection should include. |
+| Active Hour Threshold | 3 | Minimum number of XP gain events before an hour is considered fully active. |
+| Clan Members Only | Enabled | Placeholder for future external data collection that should focus on clan members. |
+
+## API usage notes
+
+No external API calls are made yet. Future heatmap data should be fetched asynchronously and cached so the game thread is never blocked. Likely sources are:
+
+- Wise Old Man for player XP snapshots and competition activity.
+- TempleOSRS as a fallback or comparison source for activity data.
+
+When those integrations are added, include clear cache lifetimes, rate-limit handling, and user-visible failure states.
+
+## Local development
+
+Use Java 11 for RuneLite compatibility:
+
+```bash
+export JAVA_HOME=/opt/data/jdks/current-java11
+export PATH="$JAVA_HOME/bin:$PATH"
+```
+
+Run tests:
+
+```bash
+./gradlew test --no-daemon -q
+```
+
+Build the plugin:
+
+```bash
+./gradlew assemble --no-daemon -q
+```
+
+Launch RuneLite in developer mode for manual testing:
+
+```bash
+./gradlew run --no-daemon
+```
+
+## Manual RuneLite testing checklist
+
+1. Start the plugin with `./gradlew run --no-daemon`.
+2. Confirm `Clan Grind Heatmap` appears in the plugin list with the expected description and tags.
+3. Enable the plugin and log in.
+4. Verify the optional login message appears when `Show Login Message` is enabled.
+5. Toggle each config option and confirm no errors appear in the RuneLite logs.
+6. Keep notes/screenshots for future Plugin Hub submission once the visible heatmap overlay/panel is implemented.
+
+## Plugin Hub prep notes
+
+Before submitting to Plugin Hub, add the real heatmap UI and screenshots/GIFs demonstrating the panel or overlay. The repo already contains the Gradle wrapper, metadata files, package naming, and smoke tests expected for a standalone RuneLite external plugin repo.
